{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1514309-homebrew-mazu-the-goddess-of-the-sea-for-the-shen","id":1514309,"title":"Homebrew: Mazu, the Goddess of the Sea [For the Shen]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-09T08:40:03-07:00","id":1514309,"title":"Homebrew: Mazu, the Goddess of the Sea [For the Shen]","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mazu, the Goddess of the Sea</b><br /> <b>Aliases: Lin Moniang, Linghui Furen, Tianfei, Tianhou</b><br /> <br /> Mazu, a newcomer to the Heavenly Bureaucracy, was once known as Lin Moniang, a seer and priestess who lived in Fujian during the 10th century. The stories about her life vary and sometimes contradict each other. Some say she was a Scion, an Incarnation of Guanyin, born into a devout family of fishers, while others believe she was a Scion of Laozi, sent to rescue those lost at sea. There are also accounts portraying her as a humble mortal who dedicated herself to helping war-time refugees from her village.<br /> <br /> During her earthly existence, Mazu exhibited exceptional religious knowledge from a young age and possessed the ability to influence rain and weather patterns along the coasts through Taoist magic. Eventually, she ascended to the heavens and received the official seal of divinity. As a goddess, she became associated with seafaring and navigation, presiding over the sea and its volatile weather patterns. Despite receiving numerous titles from successive emperors and religious leaders in recognition of her blessings, Mazu prefers to be called simply Mazu, a name that is more accessible and easier for her worshippers to use.<br /> <br /> Once, Mazu encountered two monstrous beings named Qianliyan and Shu-Feng-Er who desired her hand in marriage and sought to claim her forcefully. However, using her superior power and martial arts skills, Mazu defeated them and subdued their demonic essence. Impressed by Mazu's mercy and strength, Qianliyan and Shu-Feng-Er became her loyal companions, pledging to stay by her side. Mazu often cites their transformation as an example that even Titans, regardless of their origins, can be reformed, encouraged to abandon their destructive inclinations and embrace a path of virtue and healing.<br /> <br /> Mazu can be found anywhere in the world, extending her hand to those in need of assistance. She acts as a protector for those in danger, serving as a guiding light for those at the mercy of treacherous waters. Mazu prefers to manifest in various disguises, such as an inconspicuous fisher, a humble monk seeking alms, or an elderly woman practicing tai chi in the early morning. In all forms, she exudes wisdom and approachability, emanating a powerful aura of healing that no mortal can ignore.<br /> <br /> <b>Callings: Guardian, Healer, Sage<br /> Purviews: Beasts (Aquatic Creatures), Fortune, Health, Journeys, Passion (Mercy), Sky, Water<br /> <br /> <i>Similar to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1315401-%E3%80%8Ehomebrew%E3%80%8Fmanimekhala-the-guardian-of-the-ocean\">Manimekhala</a> post I made a long time ago, this is for Mazu, known for her popularity in her native Fujian province but also in much of southern China, Taiwan and amongst Chinese diaspora in Southeast Asia and elsewhere.</i></b></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:24:27-07:00","id":1514830,"title":"","content":"Good to see some of your exceptional work again, Svarogg!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T15:14:23-07:00","id":1518783,"title":"","content":"Nice work! My Hong Kong-set game has a scion of <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Tianhou</span></span>\u200b, and I was surprised to see her pop up here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}